k multiplicity | 0 / 1 / many `desc`; 0 / 1 / many `pakt` (**last one before `data` wins**) | overwriting assignment |\n| G. number of unknown chunks skipped | 0 / 1 / many | loop iteration count |\n| H. `chunk->size` | `0`, positive, **negative (walks backwards)**, `-16` (self-loop), `i64::MIN`, `i64::MAX` | `lib.c:115` pointer arithmetic |\n| I. `chunk` stride | **16 bytes**, not the 12 bytes real CAF uses (tail padding of `struct caf_chunk`); bytes 4..8 of each chunk are don't-care | `sizeof(struct caf_chunk)==16` |\n| J. `desc->format_id` | `== \"ima4\"` / `!=` | `lib.c:118` |\n| K. `desc->sample_rate` (`double`) | the `(ima_u64_t)double` **value** conversion has 3 hardware paths: `x >= 2^63` (bias+xor), ordered `x < 2^63` (plain `cvttsd2si`), unordered/out-of-range (`0x8000...0` indefinite). Sub-cases: `+0.0`, `-0.0`, small positive, small negative, fractional (truncation), subnormal, exactly `2^63`, `> 2^63`, `< -2^63`, `+inf`, `-inf`, qNaN, sNaN, arbitrary bit patterns | `lib.c:127` + `comisd/jae/subsd/cvttsd2si/xor` |\n| L. `desc->channels_per_frame` | any `u32`: `0`, `1`, `2`, `0xFFFFFFFF`, random | `lib.c:126` |\n| M. `pakt->frame_count` | any `u64`/`i64`: `0`, `1`, `i64::MAX`, `u64::MAX`, random | `lib.c:125` |\n| N. `data` pointer alignment | unaligned (offset 1..7) vs 8-aligned — C casts with no alignment guarantee | `lib.c:76` cast |\n| O. unread fields | `desc->format_flags/bytes_per_packet/frames_per_packet/bits_per_channel`, `pakt->packet_count/priming_frames/remainder_frames`, `caf_data->edit_count`, `ima_block` contents — must be ignored (filled with noise to prove it) | absence of reads |\n| P. `blocks` output pointer | must equal `data_chunk_ptr + 16 + 4` exactly | `lib.c:111` |\n| Q. `info->size` output | `= chunk_size` of the **`data`** chunk (s64→u64 reinterpret), *not* of the last chunk scanned | `lib.c:124` |\n\nAxis C/I/O rows are \"don't-care\" axes: every row below fills those bytes with\nseeded pseudo-random noise so that any accidental Rust read of them diverges.\n\n## Configuration rows\n\nEvery row is run through **both** `.so`s via `libloading` with **many seeded\nrandomized inputs** (count in the last column), comparing the `int` return value\n*and* all five `ima_info` fields byte-for-byte (`sample_rate` compared by\n`to_bits`), plus the pre-filled sentinel bytes of `ima_info` on error paths.\n\n| #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | iters | [x] |\n|----|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-------|-----|\n| 1  | `ima_parse` | A✗: random non-`\"caff\"` magic, everything else random | 20000 | [x] |\n| 2  | `ima_parse` | A✓ + B✗: valid magic, random `version != 1` | 20000 | [x] |\n| 3  | `ima_parse` | A✓ + B: **exhaustive** all 65 536 `version` values (only `1` proceeds) | 65536 | [x] |\n| 4  | `ima_parse` | minimal valid: `desc`,`pakt`,`data`, all chunk sizes 0, random payload fields | 5000 | [x] |\n| 5  | `ima_parse` | order `pakt`,`desc`,`data` (E) | 5000 | [x] |\n| 6  | `ima_parse` | order `desc`,`pakt`,`data` with 1 unknown chunk before `desc` (G=1) | 5000 | [x] |\n| 7  | `ima_parse` | order with 1..8 random unknown chunks interleaved at random positions (G=many, D fall-through) | 5000 | [x] |\n| 8  | `ima_parse` | multiple `desc` chunks (2..4) — **last before `data` wins** (F) | 5000 | [x] |\n| 9  | `ima_parse` | multiple `pakt` chunks (2..4) — **last before `data` wins** (F) | 5000 | [x] |\n| 10 | `ima_parse` | `data` chunk appears twice; only the first is used (break) (E,F) | 2000 | [x] |\n| 11 | `ima_parse` | non-zero positive `chunk->size` on skipped chunks, so the stride is `16 + size` (H,I) | 5000 | [x] |\n| 12 | `ima_parse` | **negative** `chunk->size` on a skipped chunk: the scan walks *backwards* into a chunk laid out earlier in the buffer (H) | 3000 | [x] |\n| 13 | `ima_parse` | `data` chunk `size` = `0` / `1` / `-1` / `i64::MIN` / `i64::MAX` / `u64::MAX` / random → `info->size` reinterpret (H,Q) | 5000 | [x] |\n| 14 | `ima_parse` | chunk padding bytes 4..8 and all unread struct fields (axis O) filled with random noise | 5000 | [x] |\n| 15 | `ima_parse` | `pakt->frame_count` = random `u64` incl. `0`,`1`,`i64::MAX`,`u64::MAX`,`0x00FF..`,`0x..FF00` (M, `ima_btoh64`) | 5000 | [x] |\n| 16 | `ima_parse` | **misaligned** `data` base pointer, offsets 1..7 (N) × valid file (all sub-offsets) | 7×2000 | [x] |\n| 17 | `ima_parse` | J✗: random `format_id != \"ima4\"` → `-3`, `info` untouched (sentinel preserved) | 20000 | [x] |\n| 18 | `ima_parse` | `desc->channels_per_frame` = random `u32` incl. `0`,`1`,`2`,`0xFFFFFFFF` (L, `ima_btoh32`) | 5000 | [x] |\n| 19 | `ima_parse` | K: `sample_rate` = **arbitrary random `u64` bit patterns** reinterpreted as `double` (covers NaN/inf/subnormal/huge, all 3 conversion paths) | 30000 | [x] |\n| 20 | `ima_parse` | K: `sample_rate` = curated hard doubles — `0.0`, `-0.0`, `1.0`, `-1.0`, `0.5`, `-0.5`, `44100.0`, `8000.0`, `2^63`, `2^63-1024`, `nextafter(2^63)`, `2^64`, `-2^63`, `-2^63-4096`, `2^63+2^11`, `1e300`, `-1e300`, `f64::MIN_POSITIVE`, `5e-324`, `+inf`, `-inf`, qNaN, sNaN, `-qNaN`, `1.5`, `-1.5`, `1e18`, `9.3e18`, `1.9e19` (exhaustive over the curated list) | 40 | [x] |\n| 21 | `ima_parse` | K×L×M×Q cross-product: random `sample_rate` bits × random `channel_count` × random `frame_count` × random `data` size, in a randomly-shaped chunk stream | 20000 | [x] |\n| 22 | `ima_parse` | P: `blocks` output pointer identity for `data` chunks at varying byte offsets in the buffer | 5000 | [x] |\n| 23 | `ima_parse` | fully randomized whole-buffer fuzz that *usually* parses: random layout, random sizes, random field values, random alignment — the composed end-to-end pipeline | 30000 | [x] |\n| 24 | `ima_parse` | `desc` present with **bad** `format_id` **and** `pakt` absent → `-3` returned before the NULL `pakt` deref (interaction of E and J) | 3000 | [x] |\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
