{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_iie6gutf6r3x5kc3g4gbgbxsuj4hpnqbqwr5kfz7tqrrsgxmixma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The MIR-level null check is inserted for raw derefs too. The right lever is the profile: the C library is compiled without UB instrumentation, so the cdylib must be too."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1570,"cache_read_input_tokens":143992,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1570,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d18ee8e3-b700-41cf-a197-c9291a65197b","uuid":"4875f990-76f9-4bb1-be0c-abe317609f60","timestamp":"2026-08-26T23:19:32.957Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_iie6gutf6r3x5kc3g4gbgbxsuj4hpnqbqwr5kfz7tqrrsgxmixma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_016z2wDZ3QS7GRoH8RSPdgdf","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-7QqEDG/translation/src/lib.rs","old_string":"// A raw dereference of a `#[repr(packed)]` field is used rather than\n// `core::ptr::read_unaligned`/`ptr::add`, because those library functions carry\n// optional \"dereferenceable and non-null\" / \"no address overflow\" UB checks\n// that are instrumented in whenever `debug-assertions` is enabled.  The C\n// library is compiled with no such instrumentation, and `ima_parse` genuinely\n// does dereference NULL for some inputs (`data == NULL`, or a `data` chunk that\n// precedes any `desc`/`pakt` chunk, leaving `desc`/`pakt` NULL).  With the\n// instrumented loads, the Rust library aborts (SIGABRT) where the C library\n// faults (SIGSEGV) -- an observable divergence.  A raw packed-field\n// dereference compiles to exactly the uninstrumented `mov` the C compiler\n// emits, in every profile.\n\n/// One-byte-aligned wrapper: reading `.0` through a raw pointer performs an\n/// unaligned, uninstrumented load.\n#[repr(C, packed)]\nstruct Unaligned<T>(T);\n\n#[inline]\nunsafe fn load_u16(base: *const u8, offset: usize) -> ima_u16_t {\n    (*(base.wrapping_add(offset) as *const Unaligned<ima_u16_t>)).0\n}\n\n#[inline]\nunsafe fn load_u32(base: *const u8, offset: usize) -> ima_u32_t {\n    (*(base.wrapping_add(offset) as *const Unaligned<ima_u32_t>)).0\n}\n\n#[inline]\nunsafe fn load_u64(base: *const u8, offset: usize) -> ima_u64_t {\n    (*(base.wrapping_add(offset) as *const Unaligned<ima_u64_t>)).0\n}\n\n#[inline]\nunsafe fn load_f64(base: *const u8, offset: usize) -> ima_f64_t {\n    (*(base.wrapping_add(offset) as *const Unaligned<ima_f64_t>)).0\n}","new_string":"// `wrapping_add` is used for the address arithmetic because the C code performs\n// unchecked pointer arithmetic that can legitimately wrap (a chunk with a\n// negative or absurd `size` moves `chunk` anywhere in the address space).\n//\n// NOTE on UB-check instrumentation: `ima_parse` genuinely dereferences NULL for\n// some inputs -- `data == NULL`, or a `data` chunk that precedes any\n// `desc`/`pakt` chunk, which leaves `desc`/`pakt` NULL when they are read at the\n// end of the function.  The C library, compiled without instrumentation, faults\n// with SIGSEGV.  Rust's optional UB checks (rustc's MIR null-check pass and the\n// `assert_unsafe_precondition!` in `ptr::read_unaligned`) would instead turn\n// those loads into a non-unwinding panic, i.e. SIGABRT -- an observable\n// divergence from the C library.  `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false` in\n// `Cargo.toml` keeps the cdylib free of that instrumentation in every profile,\n// exactly like the C build.  See `ERRORS.md` rows 4-7.\n\n#[inline]\nunsafe fn load_u16(base: *const u8, offset: usize) -> ima_u16_t {\n    core::ptr::read_unaligned(base.wrapping_add(offset) as *const ima_u16_t)\n}\n\n#[inline]\nunsafe fn load_u32(base: *const u8, offset: usize) -> ima_u32_t {\n    core::ptr::read_unaligned(base.wrapping_add(offset) as *const ima_u32_t)\n}\n\n#[inline]\nunsafe fn load_u64(base: *const u8, offset: usize) -> ima_u64_t {\n    core::ptr::read_unaligned(base.wrapping_add(offset) as *const ima_u64_t)\n}\n\n#[inline]\nunsafe fn load_f64(base: *const u8, offset: usize) -> ima_f64_t {\n    core::ptr::read_unaligned(base.wrapping_add(offset) as *const ima_f64_t)\n}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1570,"cache_read_input_tokens":143992,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1570,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d18ee8e3-b700-41cf-a197-c92