| K: 37 curated hard doubles + 15 curated hard bit patterns (`±0.0`, `±1.0`, `±0.5`, `±1.5`, `0.999…`, `44100`, `8000`, `22050`, `±48000.5`, `1e18`, `9.2e18`, `9.3e18`, `1.9e19`, `2^64`, **exactly `2^63`**, largest double `< 2^63`, just above `2^63`, `±2^63`, just below `−2^63`, `±1e300`, `f64::MAX/MIN`, `±MIN_POSITIVE`, `±5e-324`, `±inf`, qNaN, sNaN, NaN payloads), each × 8 noise fillings × alignments 0..7 | 52 × 8 | `cfg20_sample_rate_hard_doubles` | [x] |","+| 21 | `ima_parse` | K × L × M × Q cross-product (4 × 3 × 3 × 4 value classes) inside a randomly shaped chunk stream at a random alignment | 20 000 | `cfg21_cross_product` | [x] |","+| 22 | `ima_parse` | P: `info->blocks` must equal `data_ptr + data_chunk_offset + 20`, with the `data` chunk pushed to a different offset every iteration by 0..6 random skipped chunks, at random alignment | 5 000 | `cfg22_blocks_pointer_identity` | [x] |","+| 23 | `ima_parse` | end-to-end fuzz of the composed pipeline: random magic (5 % invalid), random version (5 % invalid), random `format_id` (12 % invalid), random ordering, 0..5 unknown chunks, random sizes and alignment | 30 000 | `cfg23_whole_file_fuzz` | [x] |","+| 24 | `ima_parse` | E × J interaction: `desc` present with an **invalid** `format_id` **and no `pakt` at all** ⇒ `-3` is returned before the NULL `pakt` would be dereferenced | 3 000 | `cfg24_bad_format_id_without_pakt` | [x] |","+| 25 | `ima_parse` | I: **overlapping** chunk headers — the `desc` chunk declares size 8 but has a 32-byte payload, so the next chunk header is parsed *out of the desc payload* (type = `format_id` = `\"ima4\"`, size = the `bytes_per_packet`/`frames_per_packet` pair) and lands exactly after it | 3 000 | `cfg25_overlapping_chunk_headers` | [x] |","+","+**Total: ~430 000 differential `ima_parse` invocation pairs.**","+","+## Result","+","+```","+$ cargo test --release --test phase_b_valid","+test result: ok. 29 passed; 0 failed","+```","+","+All rows pass under both the `dev` and `release` profiles and under all three","+Cargo feature configurations (see `verify.sh`)."]}],"originalFile":"# CONFIGS.md — Phase B configuration-surface table\n\n## Public entry points (complete)\n\n`c_src/include/lib.h` declares exactly one function:\n\n```c\nint ima_parse(struct ima_info *info, const void *data);\n```\n\nThere are no convenience wrappers and no lower-level exported functions — the\n`static` helpers (`ima_bswap16/32/64`, `ima_btoh16/32/64`) have internal linkage.\nThey are therefore verified *indirectly but exhaustively*: `ima_btoh16` through\nthe `version` field (all 65 536 values, row 3), `ima_btoh32` through\n`header->type` / `chunk->type` / `format_id` / `channels_per_frame` (randomized\n32-bit fuzz, rows 1/2/17/18) and `ima_btoh64` through `chunk->size` /\n`frame_count` (randomized 64-bit fuzz, rows 15/19).\n\n## Axes the C code actually branches on\n\nDerived from every `if` / `else if` / `for` / conversion in `ima_parse`:\n\n| axis | values the C distinguishes | source |\n|------|----------------------------|--------|\n| A. `header->type` | `== \"caff\"` / `!=` | `lib.c:87` |\n| B. `header->version` | `== 1` / `!=` | `lib.c:92` |\n| C. `header->flags` | **never read** (bytes 6..8 are don't-care) | — |\n| D. `chunk->type` | `\"desc\"` / `\"pakt\"` / `\"data\"` / anything else | `lib.c:97,102,107` |\n| E. chunk ordering | `desc` before/after `data`; `pakt` before/after `data`; `desc` before/after `pakt` | control flow of the `for(;;)` |\n| F. chunk multiplicity | 0 / 1 / many `desc`; 0 / 1 / many `pakt` (**last one before `data` wins**) | overwriting assignment |\n| G. number of unknown chunks skipped | 0 / 1 / many | loop iteration count |\n| H. `chunk->size` | `0`, positive, **negative (walks backwards)**, `-16` (self-loop), `i64::MIN`, `i64::MAX` | `lib.c:115` pointer arithmetic |\n| I. `chunk` stride | **16 bytes**, not the 12 bytes real CAF uses (tail padding of `struct caf_chunk`); bytes 4..8 of each chunk are don't-care | `sizeof(struct caf_chunk)==16` |\n| J. `desc->format_id` | `== \"ima4\"` / `!=` | `lib.c:118` |\n| K. `desc->sample_rate` (`double`) | the `(ima_u64_t)double` **value** conversion has 3 hardware paths: `x >= 2^63` (bias+xor), ordered `x < 2^63` (plain `cvttsd2si`), unordered/out-of-range (`0x8000...0` indefinite). Sub-cases: `+0.0`, `-0.0`, small positive, small negative, fractional (truncation), subnormal, exactly `2^63`, `> 2^63`, `< -2^63`, `+inf`, `-inf`, qNaN, sNaN, arbitrary bit patterns | `lib.c:127` + `comisd/jae/subsd/cvttsd2si/xor` |\n| L. `desc->channels_per_frame` | any `u32`: `0`, `1`, `2`, `0xFFFFFFFF`, random | `lib.c:126` |\n| M. `pakt->frame_count` | any `u64`/`i64`: `0`, `1`, `i64::MAX`, `u64::MAX`, random | `lib.c:125` |\n| N. `data` pointer alignment | unaligned (offset 1..7) vs 8-aligned — C casts with no alignment guarantee | `lib.c:76` cast |\n| O. unread fields | `desc->format_flags/bytes_per_packet/frames_per_packet/bits_per_channel`, `pakt->packet_count/priming_frames/remainder_frames`, `caf_data->edit_count`, `ima_block` contents — must be ignored (filled with noise to prove it) | absence of reads |\n| P. `blocks` output pointer | must equal `data_chunk_ptr + 16 + 4` exactly | `lib.c:111` |\n| Q. `info->size` output | `= chunk_size` of the **`data`** chunk (s64→u64 reinterpret), *not* of the last chunk scanned | `lib.c:124` |\n\nAxis C/I/O rows are \"don't-care\" axes: every row below fills those bytes with\nseeded pseudo-random noise so that any accidental Rust read of them diverges.\n\n## Configuration rows\n\nEvery row is run through **both** `.so`s via `libloading` with **many seeded\nrandomized inputs** (count in the last column), comparing the `int` return value\n*and* all five `ima_info` fields byte-for-byte (`sample_rate` compared by\n`to_bits`), plus the pre-filled sentinel bytes of `ima_info` on error paths.\n\n| #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | iters | [x] |\n|----|----------------|------------------------------------