 crashing / diverging, so the Rust must crash /","-diverge identically — they are tested by re-exec'ing the test binary in a child","-process and comparing the termination signal (or the timeout).","+implicit fault paths created by the *absence* of NULL/bounds checking (rows 4-7,","+10) and by the unbounded `for (;;)` chunk scan (rows 8-9)."," ","-| #  | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test |","-|----|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|","-| 1  | `ima_parse` | `ima_btoh32(header->type) != 'ffac'` — the first 4 bytes of `data` are not ASCII `\"caff\"` (checked *before* anything else, so version/chunks are irrelevant) | `return -1` | `err01_bad_magic` |","-| 2  | `ima_parse` | magic OK **and** `ima_btoh16(header->version) != 1` — bytes 4..6 are not big-endian `0x0001` | `return -2` | `err02_bad_version` |","-| 3  | `ima_parse` | magic + version OK, a `desc` chunk was seen before the `data` chunk, but `ima_btoh32(desc->format_id) != '4ami'` — `desc+8..12` is not ASCII `\"ima4\"`. Returns *before* `pakt` is dereferenced, so this path is safe even when `pakt == NULL`. | `return -3` | `err03_bad_format_id`, `err03_bad_format_id_no_pakt` |","-| 4  | `ima_parse` | magic + version OK and the `data` chunk is reached with **no preceding `desc` chunk** ⇒ `desc == NULL` ⇒ `desc->format_id` reads address `0x8` | SIGSEGV (NULL deref, read) | `err04_null_desc_segv` |","-| 5  | `ima_parse` | magic + version + `format_id` OK and the `data` chunk is reached with **no preceding `pakt` chunk** ⇒ `pakt == NULL` ⇒ `pakt->frame_count` reads address `0x8` | SIGSEGV (NULL deref, read) | `err05_null_pakt_segv` |","-| 6  | `ima_parse` | `data == NULL` (no null check on the buffer) ⇒ `header->type` reads address `0x0` | SIGSEGV (NULL deref, read) | `err06_null_data_segv` |","-| 7  | `ima_parse` | `info == NULL` with an otherwise fully valid buffer (no null check on the out-param) ⇒ `info->blocks = ...` writes address `0x0` | SIGSEGV (NULL deref, write) | `err07_null_info_segv` |","-| 8  | `ima_parse` | magic + version OK but the buffer contains **no `data` chunk** — the `for (;;)` scan has no bound and walks off the end of the allocation | SIGSEGV (out-of-bounds read) | `err08_no_data_chunk_segv` |","-| 9  | `ima_parse` | a non-`data` chunk whose `size == -16` ⇒ `chunk = &chunk[1] + (-16) == chunk` ⇒ the scan never advances | infinite loop (never returns) | `err09_self_referential_chunk_hangs` |","-| 10 | `ima_parse` | zero-length / truncated buffer (fewer than 8 bytes, e.g. 0..7 bytes) mapped so that reading past it faults ⇒ the header read itself is out of bounds | SIGSEGV (out-of-bounds read) | `err10_truncated_header_segv` |","+Rows 4-10 are real inputs that the C library \"handles\" by faulting or by never","+terminating, so the Rust must fault / not terminate **identically**.  They are","+verified by re-exec'ing the test binary as a child process (`crash_worker`),","+once against the C `.so` and once against the Rust `.so`, and comparing how the","+two children terminated (`WTERMSIG`, or \"still running after the timeout\").","+Rows 8 and 10 use an `mmap`'d buffer followed by a `PROT_NONE` guard page so the","+fault address is exact and deterministic rather than dependent on heap layout."," ","-## Generic FFI boundary cases (covered even though not distinct C branches)","+Tests live in `tests/phase_c_errors.rs`."," ","-| #  | case | why it is exercised | expected | test |","-|----|------|---------------------|----------|------|","-| 11 | `version` one step past the valid range: `0`, `2`, `0xFFFF`, and every other of the 65 535 invalid values (exhaustive) | `!= 1` is the only accepted value | `-2` for all but `1` | `err11_version_exhaustive` |","-| 12 | `magic` one step past valid: `\"cafe\"`, `\"cafg\"`, `\"baff\"`, `\"CAFF\"`, byte-swapped `\"ffac\"`, plus 20 000 random `u32`s | only `\"caff\"` accepted | `-1` unless exactly `\"caff\"` | `err12_magic_rando