{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jvtii3d64v2v2tbysfljbky7vp7lh3iscblsjsihdm66t55nckcq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a single translation unit exporting one function — `int ima_parse(struct ima_info*, const void*)` — which parses a CAF container to locate IMA4 audio blocks. The Rust translation was already present in `translation/src/lib.rs`.\n\n## Phase A — surface mapping\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` shows exactly one exported symbol (`ima_parse`) in both `.so`s; the diff is empty, and all Rust undefined symbols are libc/libgcc. No C module was skipped, nothing stubbed. I also verified all 7 struct layouts against a `gcc` `sizeof`/`offsetof` probe.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 10 rejection/fault rows + 6 FFI-boundary rows, derived by grepping every `return`, `NULL`, and the unbounded `for(;;)`.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 17 branch axes → 28 configuration rows.\n\n## Phase B / C — differential tests\n\nBoth `.so`s are `dlopen`ed via `libloading` and called only through `ima_parse`; the return value **and all 40 bytes** of `ima_info` (padding included, `sample_rate` bitwise) are compared. ~430 000 invocation pairs across 46 tests. The 7 fault rows (unchecked NULL `desc`/`pakt`/`info`/`data`, unbounded scan, `size == -16` infinite loop, truncation) run in child processes with `mmap` guard pages, comparing termination signals.\n\n## Bug found and fixed\n\n`err06`/`err07` failed in the **dev profile**: C died with `SIGSEGV`, Rust with `SIGABRT`. Cause: rustc's optional UB instrumentation (MIR null-check pass + `assert_unsafe_precondition!`) converts the C library's genuine NULL dereferences into a non-unwinding panic. Since the C is built without instrumentation, I disabled it via `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false` and switched the loads to `wrapping_add`. Verified load-bearing: re-enabling it re-breaks both tests.\n\n## Negative control\n\n`mutation_test.sh` injects 31 realistic mis-translations — **31/31 caught in both profiles**, including the subtle `t < 2^63` → `t <= 2^63` boundary in the `cvttsd2si` emulation. Two surviving mutants (`>=`→`>` at exactly 2^63, dropping the `is_nan` early return) are provably semantically equivalent, not blind spots.\n\nThe trickiest faithfulness detail: `conv64.u = desc->sample_rate` is a floating-point **value** conversion, not a bit-cast — the Rust reproduces gcc's exact `comisd`/`jae`/`subsd`/`cvttsd2si`/`xor 2^63` sequence (checked against `objdump`).\n\n```\nprofile=dev/release × combo=[<default>|--no-default-features|--all-features]\n  PASS build / cdylib / symbol parity / 46 tests   (all 6 configurations)\nVERIFICATION COMPLETE — all phases passed.\n```\n\nNothing in `c_src/` was modified (only the `build/` directory was added, per instructions)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3138,"cache_read_input_tokens":183760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3138,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d18ee8e3-b700-41cf-a197-c9291a65197b","uuid":"3e189821-0740-4523-a878-a8619300e796","timestamp":"2026-08-26T23:30:29.756Z"}
